    :hasEvidenceText "(GCNs) ( Kipf & Welling , 2017 ) are an efcient variant of Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) on graphs. GCNs stack layers of learned rst-order spectral lters followed by a nonlinear activation function"^^xsd:string,
        "GCN is misled by noise and mixes nodes of two classes together"^^xsd:string,
        "Our baseline is a standard GCN inspired by [9]. It is built of two GC layers as in (2). The hidden layer has 64 units and ReLU activations."^^xsd:string,
        "The graph convolutional network (GCN) is a goto solution for machine learning on graphs"^^xsd:string,
        "on Cora dataset, DeCorr improves 15-layer GCN and 30-layer GCN"^^xsd:string,
        "stacking more layers into a GCN leads to the over-smoothing problem"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :gnn,
        owl:Thing ;
    skos:skos_definition "An efficient variant of Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) on graphs that stacks layers of learned first-order spectral filters."^^xsd:string ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom "CQ_S0_R1_0016"^^xsd:string,
