    kg:textSpan "Customized Graph Neural Networks Yiqi Wang * , 1 Yao Ma * , 1 Wei Jin, 1 Chaozhuo Li, 2 Charu Aggarwal, 3 Jiliang Tang 1 1 Michigan State University 2 Microsoft Research Asia 3 IBM T. J. Watson Research Center wangy206@msu.edu, mayao4@msu.edu, jinwei2@msu.edu, cli@microsoft.com, charu@us.ibm.com, tangjili@msu.edu arXiv:2005.12386v2 [cs.LG] 14 Dec 2021 Abstract 2018; Gao and Ji 2019; Vashishth et al. 2020), and graph classication (Ying et al. 2018; Ma et al. 2019; Li et al. 2020; Gao, Liu, and Ji" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2005_12386_rag__chunk_001> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2005.12386_rag::chunk_001" ;
    kg:docId "2005.12386_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2005_12386_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "Neural Networks (GNNs) have greatly advanced the task of graph classication. Typically, we rst build a unied GNN model with graphs in a given training set and then use this unied model to predict labels of all the unseen graphs in the test set. However, graphs in the same dataset often have dramatically distinct structures, which indicates that a unied model may be sub-optimal given an individual graph. Therefore, in this paper, we aim to develop customized graph neural networks for graph classi" .

