    kg:textSpan "to train the binarized graph convolutional layers. Based on our theoretical analysis, Bi-GCN can reduce the memory consumptions by an average of 30x for both the network parameters and node attributes, and accelerate the inference speed by an average of 47x, on the citation networks. Experiments on several datasets have demonstrated that our Bi-GCN can give a comparable performance to GCN in both the transductive and inductive tasks. Besides, Our binarization approach can be easily applied to ot" .

