    kg:docId "2102.04925_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2102_04925_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "models for recommendation in a privacypreserving way. Since user interaction data is highly decentralized, there is no global user-item graph. Thus, in our method each user device locally learns a GNN model and the embeddings of user and items based on the user-item graph inferred from the local useritem interaction data on this device. The user devices compute the gradients of models and user/item embeddings and upload them to a central server, which aggregates the gradients from a number of us" .

