    kg:docId "2206.07743_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2206_07743_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "do not change much (roughly from 0.6 to 0.5). That can explain the observation in Section 5.2 why methods addressing oversmoothing perform worse than shallow GNNs while our method tackling overcorrelation can outperform them. (3) In general, with the increase of the number of layers, the learned representations becomes more correlated and more smoothing. However they show very different patterns. This observation suggests that overcorrelation and oversmoothing are different though related. Thus," .

