    kg:textSpan "not train the MLP but only focus on the forward pass of the neural network, i.e., the weights of MLP 3.3.2 Revisiting previous methods tackling oversmoothing. Since we have introduced the overcorrelation issue, next we revisit the previous methods tackling oversmoothing that have the potential to help alleviate the overcorrelation issue: (1) DropEdge [ 33 ]. DropEdge tackles the oversmoothing problem by randomly dropping edges in the graph. This can be beneficial to correlation reduction: (1) it" .

