    kg:textSpan "back-propagation, we can iteratively obtain L 2 nd / W ( k ) , k = 1 , ...K 1 and L 2 nd /W ( k ) , k = 1 , ...K . Now the calculation of the partial derivative of L 2 nd is nished. Then we continue to calculate the partial derivative of L 1 st /W ( k ) . The loss function of L 1 st can be rephrased as follows: n X 3 For simplicity of notations, we denote network representations Y ( K ) = { y ( K ) i } n i =1 as Y = { y i } n i =1 . 2 In this work, we use the sigmoid function ( x ) = 1 1+ exp ( " .

