    kg:textSpan "1 Non-Local Graph Neural Networks Meng Liu*, Zhengyang Wang*, and Shuiwang Ji, Senior Member, IEEE Abstract Modern graph neural networks (GNNs) learn node embeddings through multilayer local aggregation and achieve great success in applications on assortative graphs. However, tasks on disassortative graphs usually require non-local aggregation. In addition, we nd that local aggregation is even harmful for some disassortative graphs. In this work, we propose a simple yet effective non-local aggre" .

