    kg:textSpan "Figure 2 -(a), where m = 2 . Partitioning the input features is optional (i.e., (a) vs. (b) in Figure 2 ). We do not partition the input features within GIST so that sub-GCNs have identical input information (i.e., X ( i ) = X for all i ); see Section 5.1 . Similarly, we do not partition the output feature space to ensure that the sub-GCN output dimension coincides with that of the global model, thus avoiding any need to modify the loss function. This decomposition procedure ( subGCNs in Algorit" .

