    kg:textSpan "for common GNNs have been proven to be effective to scale to huge graphs, which can be classied into node-wise, layer-wise and graph-wise methods. Node-wise methods [ 13 , 14 , 17 ] sample a small number of neighbors for each node. Layer-wise methods [ 15 , 16 ] avoid the redundant sampling of node-wise methods. Graph-wise methods [ 19 , 20 ] partition graph and limit convolutions in smaller subgraphs. However, they require complicate implementation and may still perform redundant convolution co" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2104_13215_rag__chunk_000> a kg:Chunk ;
