    kg:textSpan "requires neighborhood sampling (Hamilton, Ying, and Leskovec 2017). Instead of using the entire l -hop neighborhood expansion N l ( v ) to perform the forward pass in an l -layer GNN, a neighborhood sampler generates a subgraph N l ( v ) of the full l -hop neighborhood N l ( v ) . Subgraph sampling is used for GNN message passing during both training and inference. The challenge presented by this approach is that no subgraph contains full neighborhood information, and this may lead to lower clas" .

