    kg:textSpan "of collaborative ltering. In addition, we also nd that using the embedding trained by walk-based models to warm start GNN models can obtain a better performance in less training time compared with pure GNN models. Figure 3 shows that, after warming up from metapath2vec model, most GNN models can reach a better performance. The GNN-based model can aggregate more interaction information from neighbors at one time and generate more informative node representations. With the help of the warm up stra" .

