    kg:textSpan "that to classify node , we only need to take the subgraph G corresponding to the receptive field of node as the input, which is generally much smaller than the whole graph. At each training step, only the predictions of the nodes in the batch contribute to the loss computation, e.g., an augmented node in each augmented graph for L . Thus, extracting the subgraphs for them to form a batch as the inputs can significantly reduce the resource requirements during training, as visualized in Fig. 6. Th" .

