    :hasEvidenceText "A graph neural network model usually consists of several GNN layers, where each layer takes the output of the previous layer as the input."^^xsd:string,
        "Any existing graph neural network model can be adapted by the Customized-GNN framework to generate sample-specic models based on the structure information."^^xsd:string,
        "As a powerful tool of learning on graph-structured data, Graph Neural Networks"^^xsd:string,
        "Despite the recent success of Graph Neural Networks (GNNs), training GNNs on large graphs remains challenging."^^xsd:string,
        "Different from CNNs handling grid data, GNNs can take nongird data as inputs. A non-grid data can be represented as a graph G = { V, E }"^^xsd:string,
        "Graph Neural Networks (GNNs)"^^xsd:string,
        "Graph Neural Networks (GNNs) are an effective framework for representation learning of graphs. GNNs follow a neighborhood aggregation scheme"^^xsd:string,
        "Graph Neural Networks (GNNs) are popular for graph machine learning and have shown great results on wide node classication tasks."^^xsd:string,
        "Graph Neural Networks (GNNs) are the rst choice methods for graph machine learning problems thanks to their ability to learn state-of-the-art level representations from graph-structured data."^^xsd:string,
        "Graph Neural Networks (GNNs) have demonstrated superior performance in learning node representations for various graph inference tasks."^^xsd:string,
        "Graph Neural Networks (GNNs), which can learn effective representations from irregular data"^^xsd:string,
        "Graph Neural Networks (GNNs), which can learn effective representations from irregular data, have given excellent performances in various graphbased tasks"^^xsd:string,
        "Modern GNNs typically adopt a neighborhood aggregation strategy by using 2322 the features and graph structures to learn discriminative node or graph representations."^^xsd:string,
        "Modern graph neural networks (GNNs) learn node embeddings through multilayer local aggregation"^^xsd:string,
        "Selfsupervised learning of graph neural networks"^^xsd:string,
        "enhancing the training of graph neural networks (GNNs)"^^xsd:string,
        "graph convolutional network (GCN) to learn node and graph representations"^^xsd:string,
        "graph neural networks (GNNs) [Kipf and Welling, 2017] that explicitly deal with the topological structures of these graph data."^^xsd:string,
        "graph neural networks (GNNs) have received much more attention and are devel"^^xsd:string,
        "leveraging a Graph Neural Network (GNN) based model to capture the spatial relationship among clients."^^xsd:string,
        "modeling rich relation information among samples, graph neural networks (GNNs) have received much more attention"^^xsd:string,
        "much effort has been devoted to generalizing neural networks to graph-structured data, resulting in the development of graph neural networks (GNNs)."^^xsd:string,
        "multi-layer Graph Neural Networks (GNNs)"^^xsd:string,
        "representations with graph neural networks (GNNs) for unsupervised scenario."^^xsd:string,
        "we propose a novel distributed algorithm for training Graph Neural Networks (GNNs)."^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :model,
        owl:Thing ;
    skos:altLabel "Graph Neural Networks"^^xsd:string,
        "GraphNeuralNetwork"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:skos_definition "A class of neural networks designed for learning on non-Euclidean space and modeling rich relation information among samples, typically adopting a neighborhood aggregation strategy."^^xsd:string ;
