    kg:textSpan "We propose GLNN , which eliminates neighbor-fetching latency in GNN inference via KD to MLP. We show GLNN s has competitive performance as GNNs, while enjoying 146-273 faster inference than vanilla GNNs and 14-27 faster inference than other inference acceleration methods. We study GLNN properties comprehensively by investigating their performance under different settings, how they work as regularizers, their inductive bias, expressiveness, and limitations. 2 R ELATED W ORK Graph Neural Networks." .

